    "q-114885": {
      "dom_id": "step-q114885",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$\\int \\frac{3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-21}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 3 & 3 & -2 & 0 & -21 \\\\  & ↓ & 9 & 21 & 63 \\\\  & 3 & 7 & 21 & 42\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-21}{x-3}=3{x}^{2}+7x+21+\\frac{42}{x-3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-21}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+7\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+21\\int \\text{d}x+42\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+\\frac{7}{2}{x}^{2}+21x+42\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-114885-a",
              "type": "math",
