    "q-114888": {
      "dom_id": "step-q114888",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3 & 0 & 2 \\\\  & ↓ & -2 & 5 & -5 \\\\  & 2 & -5 & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2}{x+1}=2{x}^{2}-5x+5-\\frac{3}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(2{x}^{2}-5x+5-\\frac{3}{x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-5{\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x+5{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-3{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{0}^{2}-\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{2}+5x\\,{|}_{0}^{2}-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({2}^{3}-{0}^{3})-\\frac{5}{2}({2}^{2}-{0}^{2})+5(2-0)-3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+1|) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}-10+10-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
